# Exercises the API gateway against the compose stack (`make up`): what it routes, what it rejects
# at the edge and what it hides. Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the
# token request stores a token for the ones after it.

@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token

### Customer token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### A public read, no token needed: Catalog's GET /products?category=phones
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/products?category=phones

### Another: Inventory's GET /stock/PHN-PIXEL-9
GET {{gateway}}/api/inventory/stock/PHN-PIXEL-9

### An authenticated route without a token: 401 at the gateway; Cart never sees it
GET {{gateway}}/api/cart/cart

### With a token: forwarded to Cart's GET /cart, Authorization untouched
GET {{gateway}}/api/cart/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A Correlation ID of your own is kept, and comes back in X-Correlation-Id
GET {{gateway}}/api/order-management/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
X-Correlation-Id: http-file-1

### A malformed one is replaced with a new UUID
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalog/categories
X-Correlation-Id: not valid!

### An internal endpoint: 404, token or not
POST {{gateway}}/api/inventory/stock/decrement
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"items": [{"variantId": "PHN-PIXEL-9", "quantity": 1}]}

### Order placement is internal too: 404
POST {{gateway}}/api/order-management/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Payment has no routes at all: 404
GET {{gateway}}/api/payment/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
